<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine of Preslav</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 900</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a> was a Bulgarian writer and churchman of the late 9th and early 10th centuries, a pupil of Methodius and one of the leading figures of the Preslav literary school under Simeon I. He composed the Didactic Gospel, a cycle of sermons, and the Alphabetical Prayer, one of the earliest poems in Slavonic. He later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Preslav.</p></div>
